Den: third-party notices
========================

Den itself is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). This file lists the third-party
software and material that Den ships in its binary, embeds, or downloads at
runtime, with the license of each.

1. What is covered, and the rule used
-------------------------------------

Go modules (section 3). A module is listed if, and only if, at least one of its
packages is linked into the released den binary: the modules reported by
`go list -deps ./cmd/den` for the release targets (GOOS=linux, CGO_ENABLED=0,
GOARCH=amd64 and arm64). Modules that appear only in `go list -m all`
(test-only helpers and other module-graph entries whose code is not compiled
into the binary) are not shipped and so have no notice here. For every listed
module the text of all LICENSE / COPYING / NOTICE / PATENTS files in the module
root is copied verbatim from the Go module cache; no license is assumed. The Go
standard library, which the toolchain compiles into every binary, is included
too. Section 3 is generated: `go run ./internal/tools/thirdparty`. A Go test
(internal/tools/thirdparty) fails when it differs from the build, so it cannot
silently go stale.

2. Skills catalogue (internal/skills)
-------------------------------------

What Den embeds: only internal/skills/catalogue.json, Den's own allowlist of
metadata (repository, pinned commit, license identifier, role tags, a
one-sentence reason, review notes, and a SHA-256 and size per file). It
contains no text or code from the skills themselves.

What Den downloads: when, and only when, the human approves an install, Den
fetches the listed files from
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/<repo>/<pinned commit>/<path>, refuses any
file whose SHA-256 differs from the catalogue, and writes them into the
project's (or agent's) own skills folder, together with the upstream license
file so the installed copy carries its notice. Nothing from these repositories
is part of the Den binary or of its release assets. Each is the work of its
authors and remains under their license:

